1
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:16,248
Oh, Corvax!

2
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,123
I'm tired.

3
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,003
Let's stop here.

4
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:22,445
Be quiet, Thimbo!

5
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,042
Look!

6
00:00:24,519 --> 00:00:25,884
There's a road.

7
00:00:26,079 --> 00:00:27,728
And cars.

8
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,921
One of the cars can take us.

9
00:00:30,199 --> 00:00:32,770
Wow! Great idea!

10
00:00:33,039 --> 00:00:35,929
Of course, it's a great idea.

11
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:38,769
Now, look in that basket.

12
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,928
We can put those clothes on.

13
00:00:43,759 --> 00:00:45,648
What about this?

14
00:00:46,399 --> 00:00:49,049
No! It's too long.

15
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,163
You're not tall enough.

16
00:00:51,359 --> 00:00:53,282
I'm taller than you.

17
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:03,569
Good morning.

18
00:01:03,759 --> 00:01:05,523
We're making a new clock.

19
00:01:06,159 --> 00:01:08,287
This is the old one.

20
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,961
I want a bigger one, please.

21
00:01:11,159 --> 00:01:13,127
Bigger than that?

22
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,489
Let's see.

23
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,841
Is this big enough?

24
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,964
That's too big.

25
00:01:20,239 --> 00:01:23,287
I want a smaller one than that.

26
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:25,369
Let's see.

27
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,799
This one's bigger than your old one.

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,968
Yes, it is.

29
00:01:33,319 --> 00:01:36,242
Oh dear! It's too heavy.

30
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,289
He can carry it.

31
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,561
He's stronger than me.

32
00:01:44,879 --> 00:01:46,324
Thank you.

33
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:50,964
Now we need two hands for the clock.

34
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:55,210
What about this?

35
00:01:55,519 --> 00:01:57,009
Let's see.

36
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,528
No. This one's too long.

37
00:02:01,879 --> 00:02:04,165
I need a shorter one.

38
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,730
Yes. This one's better.

39
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,561
Thank you.

40
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:13,447
Now the other hand.

41
00:02:14,719 --> 00:02:16,847
This looks too short

42
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,281
Take this one.

43
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,561
Yes. It's better.

44
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,368
Right!

45
00:02:25,599 --> 00:02:28,808
We are taking the shorter long one

46
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,730
and the longer shod one.

47
00:02:32,479 --> 00:02:34,527
Ah! I see.

48
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,888
How about a hat?

49
00:02:44,439 --> 00:02:45,600
Let's see.

50
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,650
I think this one looks nice.

51
00:02:49,479 --> 00:02:52,846
-What do you think? -I think it looks awful.

52
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,570
Awful!

53
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,164
It's not big enough.

54
00:02:57,919 --> 00:03:00,569
Ah! This one's better.

55
00:03:03,039 --> 00:03:04,529
Wait, Corvax!

56
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:06,919
Look!

57
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,364
Ah!

58
00:03:09,639 --> 00:03:11,322
That's better.

59
00:03:11,599 --> 00:03:13,282
Now, let's go.

60
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:30,686
Oh, thank you.

61
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:34,487
This is my daughter and her baby.

62
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,125
What's the matter, Muzzy?

63
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,130
You look ill.

64
00:03:44,319 --> 00:03:46,844
I'm not feeling well.

65
00:03:47,639 --> 00:03:49,528
What is it, Muzzy?

66
00:03:49,759 --> 00:03:52,080
I'm very hungry.

67
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,044
Stay here, Muzzy!

68
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,363
I'm going to get some clocks for you.

69
00:03:56,639 --> 00:04:00,485
I... I need my black box, too.

70
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,923
Get my black box.

71
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,203
We're going to start work.

72
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,290
Are you going to mend the clock?

73
00:04:13,479 --> 00:04:16,209
No. We're going to make a new one.

74
00:04:17,319 --> 00:04:18,889
What are you going to do?

75
00:04:19,079 --> 00:04:21,320
Well, my friend is going to help me.

76
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:23,840
We're going to take that rubbish away...

77
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:26,246
and we're going to start now.

78
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:31,650
Well, I'm going to have my tea.

79
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:40,167
It's half past five. When are you going to stop?

80
00:04:40,439 --> 00:04:42,600
Half past five?

81
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,363
I'm going to stop now.

82
00:05:01,319 --> 00:05:04,402
Wait a moment ! There's a telephone!

83
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,161
I can phone the King.

84
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:14,207
Two, double one,

85
00:05:14,519 --> 00:05:15,930
double oh.

86
00:05:18,439 --> 00:05:20,600
Two, double one, oh, oh.

87
00:05:22,439 --> 00:05:25,282
-Who is it? -It's Bob.

88
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:29,121
-It's for the King. -It's for you!

89
00:05:29,319 --> 00:05:31,686
For me? Who is it?

90
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:35,329
It's Bob. It's a call from Bob.

91
00:05:35,519 --> 00:05:36,680
From Bob!

92
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,810
Hello, Bob. Where are you?

93
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:43,088
And where's Sylvia? And where's Amanda?

94
00:05:43,439 --> 00:05:46,568
Sylvia's with Muzzy. He isn't feeling well.

95
00:05:46,759 --> 00:05:49,045
-Can you get some clocks. -What was that?

96
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:52,249
Can you get some clocks... for Muzzy?

97
00:06:05,279 --> 00:06:08,122
I'm taking this with me.

98
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:12,402
I'm taking it to her.

99
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:18,562
I'm riding from the sea. Coming back to my home.

100
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,241
Hello again, my dear.

101
00:06:21,639 --> 00:06:24,085
This is for you from me.

102
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,723
What an awful bird!

103
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:29,081
Where does it come from?

104
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,488
South America!

105
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,490
Yes. I'm writing it down.

106
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:49,289
Yes. I'm going to get Muzzy's black box.

107
00:06:50,759 --> 00:06:51,999
Of course.

108
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,766
-Did you get any clocks? -No, I didn't.

109
00:06:59,199 --> 00:07:01,280
But I phoned the King and Queen.

110
00:07:01,519 --> 00:07:04,523
They're going to get lots of clocks for Muzzy.

111
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,324
And his black box.

112
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:10,086
Ah! Entrance!

113
00:07:10,439 --> 00:07:12,088
We go in here.

114
00:07:15,839 --> 00:07:18,045
What are we going to do?

115
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:21,163
We're going to look in all the rooms.

116
00:07:21,639 --> 00:07:23,528
Be careful!

117
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:27,691
That says 'Danger. No entry.'

118
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:31,164
-We mustn't go in there. -No.

119
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:34,006
We must go this way.

120
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:41,963
Ah! Here's a box.

121
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,241
-Look! -That's it.

122
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:46,328
That's the right box.

123
00:07:46,639 --> 00:07:48,607
What does this mean?

124
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:52,407
It means it's dangerous. It isn't safe.

125
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,400
-You mustn't open it. -Aaaah!

126
00:07:59,199 --> 00:08:02,486
That was dangerous. You must be careful.

127
00:08:04,279 --> 00:08:06,122
Look! This is the way out.

128
00:08:08,199 --> 00:08:11,009
-Feeling better? -Yes.

129
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:13,200
I'm all right now.

130
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,608
Off we go!

131
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,689
I like driving.

132
00:08:24,199 --> 00:08:27,681
-You're driving too fast. -No, I'm not.

133
00:08:28,079 --> 00:08:29,922
How fast are we going?

134
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:33,249
A hundred and twenty kilometres an hour.

135
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:35,761
You mustn't go faster than a hundred.

136
00:08:36,039 --> 00:08:38,200
Look! It isn't safe.

137
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:42,281
Oh, dear! You're right.

138
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,528
I must go slower.

139
00:08:46,799 --> 00:08:48,607
How far is it?

140
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,290
How far is it?

141
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,249
A hundred and twenty metres.

142
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:06,326
It didn't go far enough.

143
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:12,645
How hot is it?

144
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:15,001
Thirty-five degrees.

145
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,288
That's too hot.

146
00:09:23,759 --> 00:09:25,363
How fast are we going?

147
00:09:25,559 --> 00:09:27,720
Fifty kilometres an hour.

148
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:31,327
That's too fast. Be careful!

149
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,680
Too late!

150
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:45,082
How far is it? Did you write it down?

151
00:09:45,279 --> 00:09:46,849
Of course I wrote it down.

152
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:49,730
Go thirty kilometres, and then"!

153
00:09:49,919 --> 00:09:52,444
Good! We're nearly there!

154
00:09:52,639 --> 00:09:54,209
Just a moment!

155
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:58,608
'Look for three big trees on the left.'

156
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:01,050
There they are!

157
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,084
Three big trees.

158
00:10:03,879 --> 00:10:06,769
'Then go right.' Look out!

159
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:11,566
Don't worry, dear!

160
00:10:11,759 --> 00:10:13,1000
I'm a very good driver.

161
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:18,043
Now. 'Straight on'.

162
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:21,528
Can you see a telephone box?

163
00:10:21,919 --> 00:10:23,330
No.

164
00:10:25,879 --> 00:10:29,361
There it is! Now go slowly.

165
00:10:30,639 --> 00:10:33,722
And look for a small road.

166
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,441
It's all right.

167
00:10:38,039 --> 00:10:39,450
There's Bob!

168
00:10:50,639 --> 00:10:53,085
What are we going to do, Corvax?

169
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,448
Where's your secret place?

170
00:10:55,639 --> 00:10:57,687
We're nearly there.

171
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:02,001
Don't worry! It's safe here.

172
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,930
-No one can see us. -I can!

173
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:06,963
I can! I can!

174
00:11:08,639 --> 00:11:11,119
She can talk.

175
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,766
I can! I can! I can!

176
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,129
What a clever baby!

177
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,606
Can she talk, then?

178
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:23,727
Shut up, Thimbo. Follow me, through...

179
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:35,440
Is that your secret place?

180
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:37,243
Yes!

181
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:41,084
It looks like an old house.

182
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:43,163
And it's very small.

183
00:11:46,679 --> 00:11:50,525
Oh! Come on, you two! Go inside!

184
00:11:54,279 --> 00:11:56,247
Put the baby down!

185
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,921
Now, press that switch!

186
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,128
Turn that handle!

187
00:12:02,519 --> 00:12:04,760
Open that door!

188
00:12:09,519 --> 00:12:10,964
There you are!

189
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,607
Look at that!

190
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,129
Wow! That's fantastic!

191
00:12:19,519 --> 00:12:21,965
Fantastic!

192
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:30,403
Lovely!

193
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,361
I'm better now.

194
00:12:34,679 --> 00:12:36,1000
Did you bring my black box?

195
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,965
Yes, we did. Here it is!

196
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:42,327
Thank you, your Majesty.

197
00:12:42,519 --> 00:12:46,160
Now I'm going to find the little princess.

198
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:48,482
With my black box.

